+## 2026-08-17 — Story 5.5: the controller demolish leg (surface decision, one-line note)
+
+- **Pad X = demolish confirm (5.5).** The pad has no pointer, so the demolish affordance rides the dpad
+  node cursor: `Node_Select` mirrors the cursor onto the selection (junction → selected, terminal → clear —
+  the same rule the click surface uses, E2 mirrored), and the pad X button (Xbox X / PS Square, the keyboard
+  X/DEL twin) confirms through the shared `Demolish` intent. No new command kinds, no per-device command
+  production — the pad emits the same intent the mouse's X key does `[FORGE #6]`. The pad has no pipe cursor,
+  so pipe demolish stays mouse/touch (click + popover button / X/DEL) until a pad pipe-highlight exists
+  (a later story); the controller leg is junction-select → X-confirm.
+
+---
